We used the blast wave function to describe the triton spectra presented in Fig. 5.3.1. Thought the fit, we were able to determine the kinetic freeze-out temperature, transverse radio flow velocity and integral the function, as well as calculate the yield of triton and \(\langle p_{T}\rangle\). The blast wave function also provided a fit for the triton spectra at different energies and centralities, which can be found in Ref. [63].

